SonarQube + Completed a SonarQube‑integrated Maven project with automated tests and quality gates.

Maven is a very solid DevOps / Java interview project.
Below is a complete step-by-step SonarQube project using Maven (Java 17). You can run this locally and also push it to GitHub.

🔹 Project Overview
Project Name: sonarqube-maven-demo
 Tech Stack:
Java 17
Maven
SonarQube
SonarScanner for Maven

Goal:
 Analyze Java code quality (bugs, vulnerabilities, code smells, coverage).
🔹 Step 1: Install Prerequisites

1️⃣ Install Java 17

java -version
If not installed:

sudo apt install openjdk-17-jdk -y

2️⃣ Install Maven

mvn -version
If not installed:

sudo apt install maven -y

3️⃣ Install & Start SonarQube (Docker – Recommended)

docker run -d \
--name sonarqube \
-p 9000:9000 \
sonarqube:lts
Access SonarQube:

http://localhost:9000
Default login

Username: admin
Password: admin

👉 Change password after login.
